WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.053
"Twenty-three, twenty-four," counted Aladdin.

2
00:00:06.054 --> 00:00:08.552
He felt for the next step with his foot.

3
00:00:08.553 --> 00:00:12.798
"Twenty-five." The stairway was dark.

4
00:00:12.799 --> 00:00:17.428
"I must be careful," he said softly to himself.

5
00:00:17.429 --> 00:00:23.427
"Thirty." Soon Aladdin saw something below in the darkness.

6
00:00:23.428 --> 00:00:28.730
"A light," he said as he slowly stepped down. "Forty-two."

7
00:00:28.731 --> 00:00:31.125
The light was getting brighter.

8
00:00:31.126 --> 00:00:35.884
"Forty-eight, forty-nine." He was almost there!

9
00:00:35.885 --> 00:00:41.165
"Fifty!" Aladdin slipped through a narrow doorway and looked around.

10
00:00:41.166 --> 00:00:45.152
"It’s the golden chamber!" he cried.

11
00:00:45.153 --> 00:00:50.920
And there stood the four golden jars, just as Magrib had said.

12
00:00:50.921 --> 00:00:54.955
"Don’t touch anything," Aladdin reminded himself.

13
00:00:54.956 --> 00:00:59.188
Just then a light wind tickled his face.

14
00:00:59.189 --> 00:01:01.876
"What’s that?" he wondered.

15
00:01:01.877 --> 00:01:07.232
A stronger wind sent the end of his sash toward a golden jar.

16
00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:11.596
"Hey!" said Aladdin, pulling his sash back.

17
00:01:11.597 --> 00:01:16.227
"I wonder if there’s a spirit in here," he whispered.

18
00:01:16.228 --> 00:01:19.510
Then Aladdin’s cap blew off.

19
00:01:19.511 --> 00:01:24.071
"Stop!" he called to no one as he jumped to catch it.

20
00:01:24.072 --> 00:01:28.480
He slid across the floor and almost hit a golden jar.

21
00:01:28.481 --> 00:01:32.982
Aladdin gulped. "That was close!"

22
00:01:32.983 --> 00:01:37.639
Holding his cap, he ran to a large door just ahead of him.

23
00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:40.061
"My name is Aladdin!" he shouted.

24
00:01:40.062 --> 00:01:42.487
"I command you to open!"

25
00:01:42.488 --> 00:01:47.702
The door swung open, and Aladdin stepped into a beautiful garden.

26
00:01:47.703 --> 00:01:52.637
The air smelled like sweet flowers and ripe fruit.

27
00:01:52.638 --> 00:01:53.841
He looked up.

28
00:01:53.842 --> 00:01:55.755
"Oranges!" he said.

29
00:01:55.756 --> 00:01:57.120
"Lemons and limes!

30
00:01:57.121 --> 00:01:59.025
Pears and plums!"

31
00:01:59.026 --> 00:02:01.369
Aladdin was getting hungry.

32
00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:04.354
He wished he could eat one of the plums.

33
00:02:04.355 --> 00:02:06.606
Then his face lit up.

34
00:02:06.607 --> 00:02:12.619
"Uncle said I can pick all the fruit I want when I have the lamp," he thought.

35
00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:16.074
The garden path was right under his feet.

36
00:02:16.075 --> 00:02:23.538
"One, two, three," he said, counting his steps as he walked between the trees.

37
00:02:23.539 --> 00:02:28.837
Exactly one hundred steps later, Aladdin arrived at the ladder.

38
00:02:28.839 --> 00:02:30.035
He looked up.

39
00:02:30.036 --> 00:02:34.240
The top was hidden high in the treetops.

40
00:02:34.241 --> 00:02:37.166
Slowly, Aladdin climbed.

41
00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:41.549
When he got to the top, the hole in the wall was in shadow.

42
00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:45.407
But Aladdin could see the lamp hanging from a chain.

43
00:02:45.408 --> 00:02:50.821
He reached in, took it, and held it in his hands.

44
00:02:50.822 --> 00:02:55.202
"It’s just a dirty, old brass lamp," he said, shaking his head.

45
00:02:55.203 --> 00:02:57.649
"I don’t want to mess up my jacket."

46
00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:03.177
So Aladdin wrapped the lamp in his sash and tucked it in his back pocket.

47
00:03:03.178 --> 00:03:07.538
Then he climbed back down the ladder.

48
00:03:07.539 --> 00:03:11.064
"Now," he said, "I’ll get something to eat."

49
00:03:11.065 --> 00:03:15.954
But when Aladdin stepped to the ground, he couldn’t believe what he saw.

50
00:03:15.955 --> 00:03:19.569
The oranges, lemons, and limes were gone.

51
00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:23.263
The pears and plums were gone too.

52
00:03:23.264 --> 00:03:28.378
Instead, the fruit trees were covered with sparkling jewels.

53
00:03:28.379 --> 00:03:32.154
"The fruit has turned to glass!" said Aladdin.

54
00:03:32.155 --> 00:03:35.525
He picked a bright-red jewel off a tree.

55
00:03:35.526 --> 00:03:38.380
"I can’t eat this," he said with a shrug.

56
00:03:38.381 --> 00:03:39.410
"But it’s pretty.

57
00:03:39.411 --> 00:03:42.688
I’ll pick the glass fruit and take it to Mother."

58
00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:47.161
Aladdin was young, and he had always been poor.

59
00:03:47.162 --> 00:03:53.352
He didn’t know these were precious gems—emeralds, diamonds, and rubies.

60
00:03:53.353 --> 00:03:55.734
They weren’t glass at all.

61
00:03:55.735 --> 00:04:02.409
He began stuffing the jewels into the pockets of his jacket and pants until they bulged.

62
00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:06.428
"Now, I must return to my uncle," he told himself.

63
00:04:06.429 --> 00:04:11.975
He hurried through the golden chamber and started up the steps toward Magrib.

64
00:04:11.976 --> 00:04:18.370
Aladdin’s load was so heavy that he could barely climb the stone stairway.

65
00:04:18.371 --> 00:04:26.235
And when he had almost reached the top, he could not get up the last step, which was taller than the others.

66
00:04:26.236 --> 00:04:33.666
"Uncle," he called out. "I’m back! Help me!"

